IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-groups`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11 Division 2: ss 372 to 374 -- the return a foreign company lodges when its documents change,
-- the financial statements it lodges (and the Registrar's powers over them), and the return about its registers. Part sgg, layer 1.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the section's own test met; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (tagged FALSE-kind);
-- NOTHING is "the text does not say" (tagged NOTHING-kind). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Time limits are counted only with sg-periods.l4; "within N days after X" of a duty is read as "not later than N days after X" (fork F-P1).

§ `Section 372: return to be filed where documents are altered`

DECLARE `s 372(1) change` IS ONE OF
    `s 372(1)(a) a change in the charter, statutes, constitution, memorandum or articles of the foreign company or other instrument lodged with the Registrar`
    `s 372(1)(b) a change in the directors of the foreign company`
    `s 372(1)(c) a change in the authorised representative or authorised representatives of the foreign company`
    `s 372(1)(ca) a change in the particulars of a director or authorised representative lodged under section 368(1)`
    `s 372(1)(d) a change in the situation or address or designation of situation or address of the registered office in Singapore, or in the days or hours it is open and accessible to the public`
    `s 372(1)(e) a change in the address of the registered office of the foreign company in its place of incorporation or origin`
    `s 372(1)(f) a change in the name of the foreign company`
    `s 372(1)(g) a change in the description of the business carried on by the foreign company`
    `s 372(1)(h) a change in the type of legal form or legal entity of the foreign company`
    `s 372(1) some other change`

DECLARE `s 372 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 372(1) lodge particulars of the change and the documents the regulations require`
    `s 372(1A) lodge a notice of the new residential address`
    `s 372(4) lodge a copy of the order`

DECLARE `s 372(1C) penalty` HAS
    `s 372(1C) the offence applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 372(1C) the maximum fine, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 372(1C) the maximum term of imprisonment, in months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 372(1C) a default penalty also applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:24101 | Return to be filed where documents, etc., altered
-- src:24103 | 372.—(1) Where any change or alteration is made in —
-- src:24105 | (a) the charter, statutes, constitution, memorandum or articles
-- src:24106 | of the foreign company or other instrument lodged with the
-- src:24107 | Registrar;
-- src:24109 | (b) the directors of the foreign company;
-- src:24111 | (c) the authorised representative or authorised representatives
-- src:24112 | of the foreign company;
-- src:24114 | (ca) the particulars of any director or authorised representative
-- src:24115 | of the foreign company which are lodged with the
-- src:24120 | Registrar under section 368(1), other than the director’s or
-- src:24121 | authorised representative’s residential address;
-- src:24123 | (d) the situation or address or designation of situation or
-- src:24124 | address of the registered office of the foreign company in
-- src:24125 | Singapore or the days or hours during which it is open and
-- src:24126 | accessible to the public;
-- src:24128 | (e) the address of the registered office of the foreign company
-- src:24129 | in its place of incorporation or origin;
-- src:24131 | (f) the name of the foreign company;
-- src:24133 | (g) the description of the business carried on by the foreign
-- src:24134 | company; or
-- src:24136 | (h) the type of legal form or legal entity of the foreign
-- src:24137 | company,
-- src:24139 | the foreign company must, within 30 days or within such further
-- src:24140 | period as the Registrar in special circumstances allows after the
-- src:24141 | change or alteration, lodge with the Registrar particulars of the
-- src:24142 | change or alteration and such documents as the regulations require.
@ref s 372(1) (src:24101-24142)
GIVEN `the change` IS A `s 372(1) change`
      `the particular that changed is the residential address of the director or authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(1) the change is one the subsection names` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the change`
    WHEN `s 372(1)(ca) a change in the particulars of a director or authorised representative lodged under section 368(1)` THEN
        (IF `the particular that changed is the residential address of the director or authorised representative`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ca) the particulars of any director or authorised representative of the foreign company which are lodged with the Registrar under section 368(1), other than the director's or authorised representative's residential address" ("other than": the residential address is dealt with by subsection (1A): fork F-O2)
         ELSE JUST TRUE)
    WHEN `s 372(1) some other change` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraphs (a) to (h) do not say "only"; a change they do not name is not covered by this subsection
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "within 30 days or within such further period as the Registrar in special circumstances allows after the change": the later of the two limits governs.
@ref s 372(1) (src:24139-24142)
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
      `the day the particulars were lodged` IS A DATE
      `the further period, in days after the change, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(1) the particulars of the change were lodged within the time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the change` `the day the particulars were lodged` (IF `the further period, in days after the change, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` GREATER THAN 30 THEN `the further period, in days after the change, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` ELSE 30) Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the foreign company must, within 30 days or within such further period as the Registrar in special circumstances allows after the change or alteration, lodge with the Registrar particulars of the change or alteration and such documents as the regulations require" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a))

@ref s 372(1) (src:24139-24142)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `the further period, in days after the change, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 372 act`
`s 372(1) the foreign company must lodge particulars of the change within 30 days or the further period the Registrar allows` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 372(1) lodge particulars of the change and the documents the regulations require`
    WITHIN (IF `the further period, in days after the change, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` GREATER THAN 30 THEN `the further period, in days after the change, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` ELSE 30)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the foreign company did not lodge particulars of the change within 30 days or the further period the Registrar allowed"

-- src:24146 | (1A) A director or an authorised representative of a foreign
-- src:24147 | company must lodge with the Registrar a notice of the director’s or
-- src:24148 | authorised representative’s new residential address within 30 days
-- src:24149 | after the date of change.
@ref s 372(1A) (src:24146-24149)
GIVEN `the day the residential address changed` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice of the new residential address was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(1A) the notice of the new residential address was lodged within 30 days after the change` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the residential address changed` `the day the notice of the new residential address was lodged` 30 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must lodge with the Registrar a notice of the director's or authorised representative's new residential address within 30 days after the date of change" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a))

@ref s 372(1A) (src:24146-24149)
GIVEN `the party who must lodge the notice` IS A `s 365 party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 372 act`
`s 372(1A) a director or authorised representative must lodge a notice of the new residential address within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the party who must lodge the notice`
    MUST `s 372(1A) lodge a notice of the new residential address`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the party who must lodge the notice` BECAUSE "the notice of the new residential address was not lodged within 30 days after the change"

-- src:24153 | (1B) Where the director or authorised representative mentioned in
-- src:24154 | subsection (1) has changed his or her residential address and has
-- src:24155 | made a report of the change under section 10 of the National
-- src:24156 | Registration Act 1965, the director or authorised representative is to
-- src:24157 | be taken to have informed the Registrar of the change of residential
-- src:24158 | address in compliance with subsection (1A).
@ref s 372(1B) (src:24153-24158)
GIVEN `the director or authorised representative has changed his or her residential address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director or authorised representative has made a report of the change under section 10 of the National Registration Act 1965` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(1B) the person is taken to have informed the Registrar of the change of residential address` MEANS
    IF `the director or authorised representative has changed his or her residential address` AND `the director or authorised representative has made a report of the change under section 10 of the National Registration Act 1965`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the director or authorised representative ... has changed his or her residential address and has made a report of the change under section 10 of the National Registration Act 1965, the director or authorised representative is to be taken to have informed the Registrar" (a "Where" gate on a deeming: marginal reading (a))

-- src:24162 | (1C) If default is made by any director or authorised representative
-- src:24163 | of a foreign company in complying with subsection (1A), he or she
-- src:24164 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:24165 | not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 372(1C) (src:24162-24165)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 372(1C) penalty`
`s 372(1C) the penalty if default is made` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (1A)`
    THEN `s 372(1C) penalty` OF JUST TRUE, JUST 5000, NOTHING, JUST TRUE   -- "he or she shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty"; no term of imprisonment is stated (NOTHING-kind (silent)); the default penalty is s 408's
    ELSE `s 372(1C) penalty` OF JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made by any director or authorised representative of a foreign company in complying with subsection (1A), he or she shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of an offence: split site (i), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S1)

@ref s 372(1C) (src:24162-24165)
GIVEN `the role of the person` IS A `s 365 role`
      `default is made in complying with subsection (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 372(1C) penalty`
`s 372(1C) the offence and its penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role of the person`
    WHEN `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` THEN `s 372(1C) the penalty if default is made` `default is made in complying with subsection (1A)`
    WHEN `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` THEN `s 372(1C) the penalty if default is made` `default is made in complying with subsection (1A)`
    OTHERWISE `s 372(1C) penalty` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If default is made by any director or authorised representative of a foreign company" names the persons it reaches, without "only"

-- src:24176 | (4) If any order is made by a court under any law in force in the
-- src:24177 | country in which a foreign company is incorporated which
-- src:24178 | corresponds to section 210 of this Act or section 71 of the
-- src:24179 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, the company
-- src:24180 | must, within 30 days or within such further period as the Registrar in
-- src:24181 | special circumstances allows after the order was made, lodge with the
-- src:24182 | Registrar a copy of that order.
@ref s 372(4) (src:24176-24182)
GIVEN `a court has made an order under a law in force in the country in which the foreign company is incorporated which corresponds to section 210 of this Act or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(4) the foreign company must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order under a law in force in the country in which the foreign company is incorporated which corresponds to section 210 of this Act or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any order is made by a court under any law in force in the country in which a foreign company is incorporated which corresponds to section 210 of this Act or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, the company must ... lodge with the Registrar a copy of that order" (a duty gated by "If": fork F-D1)

@ref s 372(4) (src:24176-24182)
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the copy of the order was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the further period, in days after the order was made, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(4) the copy of the order was lodged within the time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the order was made` `the day the copy of the order was lodged` (IF `the further period, in days after the order was made, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` GREATER THAN 30 THEN `the further period, in days after the order was made, that the Registrar in special circumstances has allowed (0 if none)` ELSE 30) Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, within 30 days or within such further period as the Registrar in special circumstances allows after the order was made, lodge with the Registrar a copy of that order" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a))

@ref s 372(4) (src:24176-24182)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 372 act`
`s 372(4) the foreign company must lodge a copy of the order within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 372(4) lodge a copy of the order`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "a copy of the order was not lodged within 30 days after it was made"

§ `Section 373: financial statements`

DECLARE `s 373(2) financial statements` IS ONE OF
    `s 373(2)(a) the financial statements the rules of the exchange require the foreign company to prepare`
    `s 373(2)(b)(i) the financial statements prepared in accordance with accounting standards substantially similar to the Accounting Standards`
    `s 373(2)(b)(ii) the financial statements prepared in accordance with the applicable accounting standards the law of the place of incorporation requires`
    `s 373(2)(b)(iii) the unaudited summary financial statements of the foreign company`

DECLARE `s 373 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 373(1) lodge the financial statements, the declaration and the statement of the auditor's name`
    `s 373(6) comply with the requirements set out in the Registrar's notice`
    `s 373(7) lodge the statements, the profit and loss account and the auditor's name in addition`

DECLARE `s 373(18) penalty` HAS
    `s 373(18) the offence applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 373(18) the maximum fine, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 373(18) the maximum term of imprisonment, in months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 373(18) a default penalty also applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 373(18A) penalty` HAS
    `s 373(18A) the offence applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 373(18A) the maximum fine, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 373(18A) the maximum term of imprisonment, in months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 373(18A) a default penalty also applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:24186 | Financial statements
-- src:24188 | 373.—(1) Subject to this section, a foreign company must lodge
-- src:24189 | with the Registrar, within the time specified in subsection (3),
-- src:24190 | financial statements made up to the end of its last financial year
-- src:24191 | together with a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that the
-- src:24192 | copies are true copies of the documents so required and, in the case
-- src:24193 | where the financial statements are audited, a statement of the name of
-- src:24194 | the auditor.
@ref s 373(1) (src:24186-24194)
GIVEN `the foreign company has lodged financial statements made up to the end of its last financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has lodged a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that the copies are true copies of the documents so required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial statements are audited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has lodged a statement of the name of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(1) the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the foreign company has lodged financial statements made up to the end of its last financial year`
       AND `the foreign company has lodged a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that the copies are true copies of the documents so required`
       AND ((NOT `the financial statements are audited`) OR `the foreign company has lodged a statement of the name of the auditor`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a foreign company must lodge with the Registrar ... financial statements made up to the end of its last financial year together with a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that the copies are true copies of the documents so required and, in the case where the financial statements are audited, a statement of the name of the auditor" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- (2) "financial statements" means: (a) where the shares are listed on an approved exchange in Singapore or a securities exchange outside Singapore
-- and the rules of the exchange require financial statements, those; (b) in any other case, (i), (ii) or (iii) in turn.
-- src:24198 | (2) In subsection (1), “financial statements” means —
-- src:24200 | (a) in the case where the foreign company’s shares are listed
-- src:24201 | for quotation on an approved exchange in Singapore or a
-- src:24202 | securities exchange in a country or territory outside
-- src:24203 | Singapore and the foreign company is required by the
-- src:24204 | rules of the approved exchange or securities exchange (as
-- src:24205 | the case may be) to prepare financial statements — those
-- src:24206 | financial statements; and
-- src:24208 | (b) in any other case —
-- src:24210 | (i) where the foreign company prepares financial
-- src:24211 | statements in accordance with accounting standards
-- src:24212 | that are substantially similar to the Accounting
-- src:24213 | Standards — those financial statements;
-- src:24215 | (ii) where the foreign company does not prepare the
-- src:24216 | financial statements mentioned in sub‑paragraph (i)
-- src:24217 | but prepares financial statements in accordance with
-- src:24222 | the applicable accounting standards as required by
-- src:24223 | the law for the time being in force in the place of the
-- src:24224 | foreign company’s incorporation which are audited
-- src:24225 | or not (as the case may be) in accordance with that
-- src:24226 | law — those financial statements; or
-- src:24228 | (iii) where the foreign company does not prepare the
-- src:24229 | financial statements mentioned in sub‑paragraph (i)
-- src:24230 | or (ii) — the unaudited summary financial
-- src:24231 | statements of the foreign company.
@ref s 373(2) (src:24198-24231)
GIVEN `the foreign company's shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange in Singapore or a securities exchange in a country or territory outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rules of the exchange require the foreign company to prepare financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company prepares financial statements in accordance with accounting standards that are substantially similar to the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company prepares financial statements in accordance with the applicable accounting standards required by the law for the time being in force in the place of its incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 373(2) financial statements`
`s 373(2) the financial statements the subsection means` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company's shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange in Singapore or a securities exchange in a country or territory outside Singapore` AND `the rules of the exchange require the foreign company to prepare financial statements`
    THEN `s 373(2)(a) the financial statements the rules of the exchange require the foreign company to prepare`
    ELSE (IF `the foreign company prepares financial statements in accordance with accounting standards that are substantially similar to the Accounting Standards`
          THEN `s 373(2)(b)(i) the financial statements prepared in accordance with accounting standards substantially similar to the Accounting Standards`
          ELSE (IF `the foreign company prepares financial statements in accordance with the applicable accounting standards required by the law for the time being in force in the place of its incorporation`
                THEN `s 373(2)(b)(ii) the financial statements prepared in accordance with the applicable accounting standards the law of the place of incorporation requires`
                ELSE `s 373(2)(b)(iii) the unaudited summary financial statements of the foreign company`))

-- (3) the time: (a) where the law of the place of incorporation requires the statements to be tabled at an annual general meeting, within 60 days after the date
-- on which the meeting is held; (b) in any other case, within the period a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside
-- Singapore would have had; that period is fixed by other sections, so the last day under them is a supplied fact.
-- src:24235 | (3) The financial statements mentioned in subsection (1) must be
-- src:24236 | lodged —
-- src:24238 | (a) in the case where the foreign company is required by the
-- src:24239 | law for the time being in force in the place of the foreign
-- src:24240 | company’s incorporation to table the financial statements
-- src:24241 | at an annual general meeting — within 60 days after the
-- src:24242 | date on which its annual general meeting is held; or
-- src:24244 | (b) in any other case — within such period as the directors of
-- src:24245 | the foreign company would have been required to lodge its
-- src:24246 | financial statements if the company were a public company
-- src:24247 | incorporated under this Act which does not keep a branch
-- src:24248 | register outside Singapore.
@ref s 373(3) (src:24235-24248)
GIVEN `the law of the place of incorporation requires the foreign company to table the financial statements at an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the last day by which the directors of a public company incorporated under this Act that does not keep a branch register outside Singapore would have been required to lodge its financial statements` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 373(3) the last day for lodging the financial statements` MEANS
    IF `the law of the place of incorporation requires the foreign company to table the financial statements at an annual general meeting`
    THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the annual general meeting is held` 60 Days
    ELSE `the last day by which the directors of a public company incorporated under this Act that does not keep a branch register outside Singapore would have been required to lodge its financial statements`

@ref s 373(3) (src:24235-24248)
GIVEN `the last day for lodging under subsection (3)` IS A DATE
      `the day the financial statements were lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(3) the financial statements were lodged within the time` MEANS
    IF `the day the financial statements were lodged` AT MOST `the last day for lodging under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The financial statements mentioned in subsection (1) must be lodged — (a) ... within 60 days after the date on which its annual general meeting is held; or (b) in any other case — within such period as the directors ... would have been required to lodge" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a))

-- (4) the Registrar may require further statements "if the Registrar is of the opinion that the financial statements ... do not sufficiently disclose the foreign company's financial position".
-- src:24252 | (4) The Registrar may, if the Registrar is of the opinion that the
-- src:24253 | financial statements mentioned in subsection (1) do not sufficiently
-- src:24254 | disclose the foreign company’s financial position, require the
-- src:24255 | company —
-- src:24257 | (a) to lodge financial statements within such period, in such
-- src:24258 | form and containing such particulars; and
-- src:24260 | (b) to annex thereto such documents,
-- src:24262 | as the Registrar may by written notice to the company require.
@ref s 373(4) (src:24252-24262)
GIVEN `the Registrar is of the opinion that the financial statements do not sufficiently disclose the foreign company's financial position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(4) the Registrar may require the foreign company by written notice to lodge further statements and annex documents` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is of the opinion that the financial statements do not sufficiently disclose the foreign company's financial position`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may, if the Registrar is of the opinion that the financial statements ... do not sufficiently disclose the foreign company's financial position, require the company" is a grant gated by "if"; the text does not close the gate with "only if" (the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)

-- (5) subsection (4) does not authorise the Registrar to require what a public company incorporated under this Act would not have to furnish.
-- src:24267 | (5) Subsection (4) does not authorise the Registrar to require —
-- src:24269 | (a) financial statements to contain any particulars; or
-- src:24274 | (b) the company to annex, attach or to send any documents,
-- src:24276 | that would not be required to be furnished if the company were a
-- src:24277 | public company incorporated under this Act.
@ref s 373(5) (src:24267-24277)
GIVEN `a public company incorporated under this Act would not be required to furnish the particulars or documents the Registrar requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(5) subsection (4) does not authorise the Registrar to require the particulars or documents` MEANS
    IF `a public company incorporated under this Act would not be required to furnish the particulars or documents the Registrar requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- "Subsection (4) does not authorise the Registrar to require — (a) financial statements to contain any particulars; or (b) the company to annex, attach or to send any documents, that would not be required to be furnished if the company were a public company incorporated under this Act" (a flat negative: it counts as the text's no, N2 of 2026-11-04)
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection removes the authority only for what a public company would not have to furnish; for anything else it says nothing

-- (6) the foreign company must comply with the requirements set out in the notice under (4); the notice sets its own time.
-- src:24281 | (6) The foreign company must comply with the requirements set
-- src:24282 | out in the notice under subsection (4).
@ref s 373(6) (src:24281-24282)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the foreign company a notice under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has complied with the requirements set out in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(6) the foreign company has complied with the requirements in the notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has given the foreign company a notice under subsection (4)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The foreign company must comply with the requirements set out in the notice under subsection (4)" speaks only where such a notice has been given
    ELSE (IF `the foreign company has complied with the requirements set out in the notice`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The foreign company must comply with the requirements set out in the notice under subsection (4)" (a duty not met)

@ref s 373(6) (src:24281-24282)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 373 act`
`s 373(6) the foreign company must comply with the requirements in the Registrar's notice within the period the notice gives` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 373(6) comply with the requirements set out in the Registrar's notice`
    WITHIN `the number of days the notice allows`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the foreign company did not comply with the requirements in the Registrar's notice within the period the notice allowed"

-- (7) in addition: (a) a duly audited statement of assets used in and liabilities arising out of its operations in Singapore; (b) a duly audited profit and loss account
-- for the last preceding financial year; (c) a statement of the name of the auditor who audited (a) or (b) or both; within the time specified in subsection (3).
-- src:24286 | (7) In addition to the financial statements required to be lodged with
-- src:24287 | the Registrar under subsections (1), (3) and (4), a foreign company
-- src:24288 | must lodge with the Registrar within the time specified in
-- src:24289 | subsection (3) the following:
-- src:24291 | (a) a duly audited statement showing its assets used in and
-- src:24292 | liabilities arising out of its operations in Singapore as at the
-- src:24293 | date to which its balance sheet was made up;
-- src:24295 | (b) a duly audited profit and loss account for the last preceding
-- src:24296 | financial year of the company;
-- src:24302 | (c) a statement of the name of the auditor who audited the
-- src:24303 | documents referred to in paragraph (a) or (b), or both
-- src:24304 | paragraphs (a) and (b), as the case may be.
@ref s 373(7) (src:24286-24304)
GIVEN `the foreign company has lodged a duly audited statement showing its assets used in and liabilities arising out of its operations in Singapore as at the date to which its balance sheet was made up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has lodged a duly audited profit and loss account for the last preceding financial year of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has lodged a statement of the name of the auditor who audited the documents referred to in paragraph (a) or (b), or both` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(7) the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires in addition` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company has lodged a duly audited statement showing its assets used in and liabilities arising out of its operations in Singapore as at the date to which its balance sheet was made up` AND `the foreign company has lodged a duly audited profit and loss account for the last preceding financial year of the company` AND `the foreign company has lodged a statement of the name of the auditor who audited the documents referred to in paragraph (a) or (b), or both`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In addition to the financial statements required to be lodged ..., a foreign company must lodge with the Registrar within the time specified in subsection (3) the following: (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ..." (a duty not met: the provision's own question; the alternatives of subsections (9), (12), (13A) and (17) are other functions)

@ref s 373(7) (src:24286-24289)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from now to the last day for lodging under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 373 act`
`s 373(7) the foreign company must lodge the audited statement, the audited profit and loss account and the auditor's name within the time in subsection (3)` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 373(7) lodge the statements, the profit and loss account and the auditor's name in addition`
    WITHIN `the number of days from now to the last day for lodging under subsection (3)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the audited statement, the audited profit and loss account and the auditor's name were not lodged within the time specified in subsection (3)"

-- src:24310 | (7A) A foreign company which lodges with the Registrar a duly
-- src:24311 | audited profit and loss account under subsection (7)(b) must ensure
-- src:24312 | that, insofar as is practicable, the profit and loss account complies
-- src:24313 | with the requirements of the Accounting Standards and gives a true
-- src:24314 | and fair view of the profit or loss arising out of the company’s
-- src:24315 | operation in Singapore for the last preceding financial year of the
-- src:24316 | company.
@ref s 373(7A) (src:24310-24316)
GIVEN `the foreign company has lodged a duly audited profit and loss account under subsection (7)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the profit and loss account complies, insofar as is practicable, with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the profit and loss account gives a true and fair view of the profit or loss arising out of the company's operation in Singapore for the last preceding financial year of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(7A) the foreign company has ensured that the profit and loss account complies and gives a true and fair view` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign company has lodged a duly audited profit and loss account under subsection (7)(b)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A foreign company which lodges with the Registrar a duly audited profit and loss account under subsection (7)(b) must ensure" speaks only of one which lodges it
    ELSE (IF `the profit and loss account complies, insofar as is practicable, with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` AND `the profit and loss account gives a true and fair view of the profit or loss arising out of the company's operation in Singapore for the last preceding financial year of the company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ensure that, insofar as is practicable, the profit and loss account complies with the requirements of the Accounting Standards and gives a true and fair view" (a duty not met)

-- (8) "entitled to make such apportionments of expenses ... and to add such notes and explanations as in its opinion are necessary or desirable": an entitlement (fork F-E1).
-- src:24320 | (8) For the purpose of subsection (7A), the foreign company is
-- src:24321 | entitled to make such apportionments of expenses incurred in
-- src:24322 | connection with operations or administration affecting both
-- src:24323 | Singapore and elsewhere and to add such notes and explanations as
-- src:24328 | in its opinion are necessary or desirable in order to give a true and fair
-- src:24329 | view of the profit or loss of its operations in Singapore.
@ref s 373(8) (src:24320-24329)
GIVEN `the purpose is to comply with subsection (7A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company apportions expenses incurred in connection with operations or administration affecting both Singapore and elsewhere, or adds notes and explanations, that in its opinion are necessary or desirable to give a true and fair view of the profit or loss of its operations in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(8) the foreign company is entitled to make the apportionments and add the notes and explanations` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is to comply with subsection (7A)` AND `the foreign company apportions expenses incurred in connection with operations or administration affecting both Singapore and elsewhere, or adds notes and explanations, that in its opinion are necessary or desirable to give a true and fair view of the profit or loss of its operations in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of subsection (7A), the foreign company is entitled to make such apportionments ... and to add such notes and explanations as in its opinion are necessary or desirable": the entitlement is for that purpose and those acts, and says nothing of others

-- (9) a dormant foreign company "may, in lieu of satisfying the requirements of subsection (7)", lodge unaudited documents.
-- src:24335 | (9) A foreign company which is dormant in Singapore may, in lieu
-- src:24336 | of satisfying the requirements of subsection (7), lodge with the
-- src:24337 | Registrar —
-- src:24339 | (a) an unaudited statement showing its assets used in and
-- src:24340 | liabilities arising out of its operations in Singapore; and
-- src:24342 | (b) an unaudited profit and loss account with respect to the
-- src:24343 | company’s operations in Singapore.
@ref s 373(9) (src:24335-24343)
GIVEN `the foreign company is dormant in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(9) the foreign company may lodge unaudited documents in lieu of subsection (7)` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company is dormant in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A foreign company which is dormant in Singapore may, in lieu of satisfying the requirements of subsection (7), lodge" names the companies it grants the option to, without "only"

-- (10) the Registrar may, on application and payment of the prescribed application fee, extend the period in (3) for any or all of the requirements of (3)(b) and (7).
-- src:24347 | (10) The Registrar may, on application by a foreign company and
-- src:24348 | payment of the prescribed application fee, extend the period referred
-- src:24349 | to in subsection (3) within which the company is required to comply
-- src:24350 | with any or all of the requirements of subsections (3)(b) and (7).
@ref s 373(10) (src:24347-24350)
GIVEN `the foreign company has applied for an extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has paid the prescribed application fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is one of subsection (3)(b) or subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(10) the Registrar may extend the period for the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the foreign company has applied for an extension` AND `the foreign company has paid the prescribed application fee`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may, on application by a foreign company and payment of the prescribed application fee, extend the period" (a "may" gated by "on application": split site (ii), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S3)
    ELSE (IF `the requirement is one of subsection (3)(b) or subsection (7)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "extend the period referred to in subsection (3) within which the company is required to comply with any or all of the requirements of subsections (3)(b) and (7)": a requirement outside those is not covered

-- (11) deemed duly audited "if it is accompanied by a report by an accounting entity appointed to provide auditing services in respect of the foreign company's
-- operations in Singapore which complies, insofar as is practicable, with section 207". "Accounting entity" is s 4(1)'s.
-- src:24354 | (11) A statement and profit and loss account is deemed to have been
-- src:24355 | duly audited for the purposes of subsection (7) if it is accompanied by
-- src:24356 | a report by an accounting entity appointed to provide auditing
-- src:24357 | services in respect of the foreign company’s operations in Singapore
-- src:24358 | which complies, insofar as is practicable, with section 207.
@ref s 373(11) (src:24354-24358)
GIVEN `the report is by a public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is by an accounting corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is by an accounting firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is by an accounting limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounting entity was appointed to provide auditing services in respect of the foreign company's operations in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report complies, insofar as is practicable, with section 207` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(11) the statement and profit and loss account are deemed to have been duly audited` MEANS
    IF    `s 4(1) "accounting entity" the person is an accounting entity` `the report is by a public accountant` `the report is by an accounting corporation` `the report is by an accounting firm` `the report is by an accounting limited liability partnership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the accounting entity was appointed to provide auditing services in respect of the foreign company's operations in Singapore`
       AND `the report complies, insofar as is practicable, with section 207`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A statement and profit and loss account is deemed to have been duly audited for the purposes of subsection (7) if it is accompanied by a report by an accounting entity appointed to provide auditing services ... which complies, insofar as is practicable, with section 207" (a deeming gated by "if": marginal reading (a); the other reading is NOTHING, since a statement may be duly audited in some other way)

-- (12) waiver: "upon the written application" and "if the Registrar is satisfied that" one of four things.
-- src:24362 | (12) The Registrar may, upon the written application of a foreign
-- src:24363 | company, waive the requirement of a foreign company to lodge the
-- src:24364 | documents referred to in subsection (7)(a), (b) and (c) if the Registrar
-- src:24365 | is satisfied that —
-- src:24367 | (a) it is impractical for the foreign company to comply having
-- src:24368 | regard to the nature of the foreign company’s operations in
-- src:24369 | Singapore;
-- src:24371 | (b) it would be of no real value having regard to the amount
-- src:24372 | involved;
-- src:24374 | (c) it would involve expense unduly out of proportion to its
-- src:24375 | value; or
-- src:24380 | (d) it would be misleading or harmful to the business of the
-- src:24381 | foreign company, or to any company which is deemed by
-- src:24382 | virtue of section 6 to be related to the foreign company.
@ref s 373(12) (src:24362-24382)
GIVEN `the foreign company has applied in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it is impractical for the foreign company to comply having regard to the nature of its operations in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be of no real value having regard to the amount involved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would involve expense unduly out of proportion to its value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be misleading or harmful to the business of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be misleading or harmful to the business of the other company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other corporation is deemed to be related to the corporation by virtue of section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(12) the Registrar may waive the requirement to lodge the documents referred to in subsection (7)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign company has applied in writing`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may, upon the written application of a foreign company, waive the requirement" (a "may" gated by "upon": split site (ii), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S3)
    ELSE (IF    `the Registrar is satisfied that it is impractical for the foreign company to comply having regard to the nature of its operations in Singapore`
             OR `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be of no real value having regard to the amount involved`
             OR `the Registrar is satisfied that it would involve expense unduly out of proportion to its value`
             OR `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be misleading or harmful to the business of the foreign company`
             OR (`the Registrar is satisfied that it would be misleading or harmful to the business of the other company` AND `s 4(1) "related corporation" the other corporation is a related corporation of the corporation` `the other corporation is deemed to be related to the corporation by virtue of section 6` EQUALS JUST TRUE)   -- the seam of PLAN section 4 (B): a company deemed by section 6 to be related to the foreign company is asked of the keel's function
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Registrar is satisfied that — (a) ... (d) ..." is a gate on a grant that the text does not close with "only if" (the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)

-- (13) an order on application: relief from the form and content of the statements of subsection (2)(b), or leave to lodge another document instead.
-- src:24386 | (13) The Registrar may, upon the application of a foreign company,
-- src:24387 | make an order —
-- src:24389 | (a) relieving the foreign company from complying with any
-- src:24390 | requirement relating to the form and content of the
-- src:24391 | financial statements mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(i) or
-- src:24392 | (ii) or the unaudited summary financial statements
-- src:24393 | mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(iii), including any aspect
-- src:24394 | relating to the audit of those documents; or
-- src:24396 | (b) allowing the foreign company to lodge under
-- src:24397 | subsection (1) any other document instead of the
-- src:24398 | financial statements mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(i) or
-- src:24399 | (ii) or the unaudited summary financial statements
-- src:24400 | mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(iii).
@ref s 373(13) (src:24386-24400)
GIVEN `the foreign company has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial statements are those mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (ii), or the unaudited summary financial statements mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(iii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(13) the Registrar may make the order on the application` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign company has applied`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may, upon the application of a foreign company, make an order" (a "may" gated by "upon": split site (ii), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S3)
    ELSE (IF `the financial statements are those mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (ii), or the unaudited summary financial statements mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(iii)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order relieves from "the financial statements mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (ii) or the unaudited summary financial statements mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(iii)"; statements of subsection (2)(a) are outside it

-- src:24404 | (13A) The Registrar may, upon the application of a foreign
-- src:24405 | company, make an order relieving the foreign company from any
-- src:24406 | requirement relating to audit or the form and content of the
-- src:24407 | documents referred to in subsection (7) or (7A).
@ref s 373(13A) (src:24404-24407)
GIVEN `the foreign company has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to audit or to the form and content of the documents referred to in subsection (7) or (7A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(13A) the Registrar may make the order relieving the foreign company from the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign company has applied`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may, upon the application of a foreign company, make an order relieving the foreign company from any requirement relating to audit or the form and content of the documents referred to in subsection (7) or (7A)" (a "may" gated by "upon": split site (ii), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S3)
    ELSE (IF `the requirement relates to audit or to the form and content of the documents referred to in subsection (7) or (7A)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the relief is "from any requirement relating to audit or the form and content of the documents referred to in subsection (7) or (7A)"

-- src:24413 | (14) The Registrar may make the order mentioned in
-- src:24414 | subsection (13) or (13A) unconditionally or subject to the
-- src:24415 | condition that the foreign company comply with such other
-- src:24416 | requirements relating to audit or the form and content of the
-- src:24417 | documents as the Registrar may determine.
@ref s 373(14) (src:24413-24417)
GIVEN `the order is the order mentioned in subsection (13) or (13A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(14) the Registrar may make the order unconditionally or subject to conditions` MEANS
    IF `the order is the order mentioned in subsection (13) or (13A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may make the order mentioned in subsection (13) or (13A) unconditionally or subject to the condition that the foreign company comply with such other requirements" speaks of that order only

-- (15) "must not make an order under subsection (13) or (13A) unless the Registrar is of the opinion that ...": a bar, so the answer is the bar.
-- src:24423 | (15) The Registrar must not make an order under subsection (13) or
-- src:24424 | (13A) unless the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance with the
-- src:24425 | requirements of this section would render the documents misleading
-- src:24430 | or inappropriate to the circumstances of the foreign company or
-- src:24431 | would impose unreasonable burdens on the company.
@ref s 373(15) (src:24423-24431)
GIVEN `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance with the requirements of the section would render the documents misleading or inappropriate to the circumstances of the foreign company or would impose unreasonable burdens on the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(15) the Registrar is barred from making an order under subsection (13) or (13A)` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance with the requirements of the section would render the documents misleading or inappropriate to the circumstances of the foreign company or would impose unreasonable burdens on the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar must not make an order ... unless the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance ... would render the documents misleading or inappropriate ... or would impose unreasonable burdens": once the opinion is formed the bar lifts, and the subsection grants no power
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies: "must not make an order under subsection (13) or (13A) unless" (a flat negative with "unless")

-- src:24437 | (16) The Registrar may make an order under subsection (13) or
-- src:24438 | (13A) which may be limited to a specific period and may from time to
-- src:24439 | time revoke or suspend the operation of any such order.
@ref s 373(16) (src:24437-24439)
GIVEN `the order is an order made under subsection (13) or (13A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(16) the order may be limited to a specific period and may be revoked or suspended from time to time` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order made under subsection (13) or (13A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may make an order under subsection (13) or (13A) which may be limited to a specific period and may from time to time revoke or suspend the operation of any such order" speaks of those orders only

-- (17) the Minister's orders: substitute other accounting standards, or exempt a class from subsection (7) or (7A). Whether an order exists is a supplied fact.
-- src:24445 | (17) Without affecting subsections (12), (13), (13A) and (14), the
-- src:24446 | Minister may, by order in the Gazette, in respect of foreign companies
-- src:24447 | of a specified class or description —
-- src:24449 | (a) substitute other accounting standards for the Accounting
-- src:24450 | Standards, and the provisions of this section apply
-- src:24451 | accordingly in respect of such foreign companies; or
-- src:24453 | (b) exempt foreign companies of a specified class or
-- src:24454 | description from any or all of the requirements of
-- src:24455 | subsection (7) or (7A).
@ref s 373(17) (src:24445-24455)
GIVEN `the Minister has by order in the Gazette substituted other accounting standards for the Accounting Standards for foreign companies of a specified class or description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company is of that class or description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(17)(a) the other accounting standards apply to the foreign company in place of the Accounting Standards` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has by order in the Gazette substituted other accounting standards for the Accounting Standards for foreign companies of a specified class or description` AND `the foreign company is of that class or description`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Minister's order is not among the sources, and the text does not say there is one

@ref s 373(17) (src:24445-24455)
GIVEN `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted foreign companies of a specified class or description from any or all of the requirements of subsection (7) or (7A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company is of that class or description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(17)(b) the foreign company is exempt from the requirements of subsection (7) or (7A) the order names` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted foreign companies of a specified class or description from any or all of the requirements of subsection (7) or (7A)` AND `the foreign company is of that class or description`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Minister's order is not among the sources, and the text does not say there is one

-- src:24463 | (18) If default is made by a foreign company in complying with this
-- src:24464 | section, other than subsection (7A) —
-- src:24466 | (a) the company; and
-- src:24468 | (b) every director or equivalent person, and every authorised
-- src:24469 | representative of the company, who knowingly and
-- src:24470 | wilfully authorises or permits the default,
-- src:24472 | shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:24473 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000.
@ref s 373(18) (src:24463-24473)
GIVEN `the elements of the offence are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 373(18) penalty`
`s 373(18) the penalty if the element is met` MEANS
    IF `the elements of the offence are met`
    THEN `s 373(18) penalty` OF JUST TRUE, JUST 10000, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- "shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000"; no term of imprisonment and no default penalty is stated (NOTHING-kind (silent))
    ELSE `s 373(18) penalty` OF JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made by a foreign company in complying with this section, other than subsection (7A) — (a) the company; and (b) every director or equivalent person, and every authorised representative of the company, who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default, shall each be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of an offence: split site (i), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S1)

-- (18) default in complying with the section, other than subsection (7A): the company; every director or equivalent person and every authorised representative who knowingly
-- and wilfully authorises or permits the default; each a fine not exceeding $10,000.
@ref s 373(18) (src:24463-24473)
GIVEN `the role of the person` IS A `s 365 role`
      `default is made by the foreign company in complying with section 373, other than subsection (7A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 373(18) penalty`
`s 373(18) the offence and its penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role of the person`
    WHEN `s 365 role: the foreign company` THEN `s 373(18) the penalty if the element is met` `default is made by the foreign company in complying with section 373, other than subsection (7A)`
    WHEN `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` THEN `s 373(18) the penalty if the element is met` (`default is made by the foreign company in complying with section 373, other than subsection (7A)` AND `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default`)
    WHEN `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` THEN `s 373(18) the penalty if the element is met` (`default is made by the foreign company in complying with section 373, other than subsection (7A)` AND `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default`)
    OTHERWISE `s 373(18) penalty` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) the company; and (b) every director or equivalent person, and every authorised representative of the company, who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default" names the persons it reaches, without "only"

-- (18A) default in complying with subsection (7A): the company, a fine not exceeding $250,000; each director or equivalent person or authorised representative who knowingly and wilfully
-- authorises or permits it: (i) a fine not exceeding $250,000; or (ii) if the offence was committed with intent to defraud the creditors of the company or of any other person, or for a
-- fraudulent purpose, a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 3 years or both.
-- src:24481 | (18A) If default is made by a foreign company in complying with
-- src:24482 | subsection (7A) —
-- src:24487 | (a) the company shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:24488 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $250,000; and
-- src:24490 | (b) every director or equivalent person, and every authorised
-- src:24491 | representative, of the company, who knowingly and
-- src:24492 | wilfully authorises or permits the default, shall each be
-- src:24493 | guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:24494 | conviction —
-- src:24496 | (i) to a fine not exceeding $250,000; or
-- src:24498 | (ii) if the offence was committed with intent to defraud
-- src:24499 | the creditors of the company or creditors of any other
-- src:24500 | person, or for a fraudulent purpose, to a fine not
-- src:24501 | exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term
-- src:24502 | not exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 373(18A) (src:24481-24502)
GIVEN `the elements of the offence are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence was committed with intent to defraud the creditors of the company or creditors of any other person, or for a fraudulent purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 373(18A) penalty`
`s 373(18A) the penalty if the element is met` MEANS
    IF NOT `the elements of the offence are met`
    THEN `s 373(18A) penalty` OF JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made by a foreign company in complying with subsection (7A) — (a) the company shall be guilty of an offence ...; and (b) every director or equivalent person, and every authorised representative, of the company, who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default, shall each be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of an offence: split site (i), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S1)
    ELSE (IF `the person is the foreign company` OR (NOT `the offence was committed with intent to defraud the creditors of the company or creditors of any other person, or for a fraudulent purpose`)
          THEN `s 373(18A) penalty` OF JUST TRUE, JUST 250000, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- (a) the company: a fine not exceeding $250,000; (b)(i) the individual: a fine not exceeding $250,000; no term of imprisonment is stated (NOTHING-kind (silent))
          ELSE `s 373(18A) penalty` OF JUST TRUE, JUST 250000, JUST 36, NOTHING)   -- (b)(ii) "to a fine not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both": 3 years is 36 months

@ref s 373(18A) (src:24481-24502)
GIVEN `the role of the person` IS A `s 365 role`
      `default is made by the foreign company in complying with subsection (7A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence was committed with intent to defraud the creditors of the company or creditors of any other person, or for a fraudulent purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 373(18A) penalty`
`s 373(18A) the offence and its penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role of the person`
    WHEN `s 365 role: the foreign company` THEN `s 373(18A) the penalty if the element is met` `default is made by the foreign company in complying with subsection (7A)` `the offence was committed with intent to defraud the creditors of the company or creditors of any other person, or for a fraudulent purpose` TRUE
    WHEN `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` THEN `s 373(18A) the penalty if the element is met` (`default is made by the foreign company in complying with subsection (7A)` AND `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default`) `the offence was committed with intent to defraud the creditors of the company or creditors of any other person, or for a fraudulent purpose` FALSE
    WHEN `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` THEN `s 373(18A) the penalty if the element is met` (`default is made by the foreign company in complying with subsection (7A)` AND `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default`) `the offence was committed with intent to defraud the creditors of the company or creditors of any other person, or for a fraudulent purpose` FALSE
    OTHERWISE `s 373(18A) penalty` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) the company ...; and (b) every director or equivalent person, and every authorised representative, of the company, who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default" names the persons it reaches, without "only"

-- (19) the definitions the section uses.
-- src:24508 | (19) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:24510 | (a) a foreign company is dormant in Singapore during a period
-- src:24511 | in which no accounting transaction arising out of its
-- src:24512 | operations in Singapore occurs; and the company ceases to
-- src:24513 | be dormant on the occurrence of such a transaction; and
@ref s 373(19)(a) (src:24508-24513)
GIVEN `no accounting transaction arising out of the foreign company's operations in Singapore occurs during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(19)(a) the foreign company is dormant in Singapore during the period` MEANS
    IF `no accounting transaction arising out of the foreign company's operations in Singapore occurs during the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a foreign company is dormant in Singapore during a period in which no accounting transaction arising out of its operations in Singapore occurs; and the company ceases to be dormant on the occurrence of such a transaction"

-- src:24515 | (b) an “accounting transaction” means a transaction for which
-- src:24516 | accounting or other records would be required to be kept so
-- src:24517 | as to enable the documents referred to in subsection (7) to
-- src:24518 | be prepared.
@ref s 373(19)(b) (src:24515-24518)
GIVEN `the transaction is one for which accounting or other records would be required to be kept so as to enable the documents referred to in subsection (7) to be prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 373(19)(b) the transaction is an accounting transaction` MEANS
    IF `the transaction is one for which accounting or other records would be required to be kept so as to enable the documents referred to in subsection (7) to be prepared`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an “accounting transaction” means a transaction for which accounting or other records would be required to be kept so as to enable the documents referred to in subsection (7) to be prepared" (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 374: return about the keeping of registers`

DECLARE `s 374 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 374 lodge a return containing the prescribed information about the keeping of the registers`

-- src:24522 | Return to be filed on keeping of registers of foreign company
-- src:24524 | 374. A foreign company must, at the time when making a lodgment
-- src:24525 | of —
-- src:24527 | (a) its financial statements in accordance with section 373(1);
-- src:24528 | or
-- src:24530 | (b) where the Registrar allows under section 373(13)(b) the
-- src:24531 | foreign company to lodge under section 373(1) any other
-- src:24532 | document instead of its financial statements — that other
-- src:24533 | document,
-- src:24538 | also lodge with the Registrar a return containing prescribed
-- src:24539 | information relating to the keeping of the following registers:
-- src:24541 | (c) the register of controllers kept by the foreign company
-- src:24542 | under section 386AF;
-- src:24544 | (d) the register of nominee directors kept by the foreign
-- src:24545 | company under section 386AKA;
-- src:24547 | (e) the register of nominee shareholders kept by the foreign
-- src:24548 | company under section 386ALA.
@ref s 374 (src:24522-24548)
GIVEN `the lodgment is of the financial statements in accordance with section 373(1), or of another document the Registrar allows under section 373(13)(b) instead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return containing the prescribed information about the register of controllers under section 386AF is lodged at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return containing the prescribed information about the register of nominee directors under section 386AKA is lodged at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return containing the prescribed information about the register of nominee shareholders under section 386ALA is lodged at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 374 the foreign company has lodged the return with its lodgment` MEANS
    IF NOT `the lodgment is of the financial statements in accordance with section 373(1), or of another document the Registrar allows under section 373(13)(b) instead`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A foreign company must, at the time when making a lodgment of — (a) its financial statements in accordance with section 373(1); or (b) ... that other document, also lodge ... a return" speaks of those lodgments only
    ELSE (IF `the return containing the prescribed information about the register of controllers under section 386AF is lodged at the same time` AND `the return containing the prescribed information about the register of nominee directors under section 386AKA is lodged at the same time` AND `the return containing the prescribed information about the register of nominee shareholders under section 386ALA is lodged at the same time`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "also lodge with the Registrar a return containing prescribed information relating to the keeping of the following registers: (c) the register of controllers ...; (d) the register of nominee directors ...; (e) the register of nominee shareholders ..." (a duty not met; the prescribed information is a supplied fact)

@ref s 374 (src:24524-24548)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 374 act`
`s 374 the foreign company must lodge the return when it lodges its financial statements` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 374 lodge a return containing the prescribed information about the keeping of the registers`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 374 states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the return about the keeping of the registers was not lodged" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]
